  "limits": [
    "Acceptance delivers the exact production render Runnable captured at mocked Thread construction/start on the fixture owner. Android builders, AudioTrack and static calls are inert; no real worker, native allocation, playback or audio occurs.",
    "Controlled deferred Runnable and track-interaction histories establish lifetime and cleanup regressions. Actual thread scheduling, blocking builder, the 500ms join timeout, native/API28/29, optimized worker and audio quality remain unverified.",
    "Already admitted play or an in-progress chunk write can race retirement. No universal cancellation or play-vs-stop ordering promise is made. The 500ms join argument does not guarantee completion of platform stop/release within 500ms.",
    "Atomic track claim gives one cleanup owner; stop and release are independent best-effort attempts. Platform cleanup failures/completion and stop-throws behavior are not native acceptance; release-after-stop-failure is source-reviewed only.",
    "Public start/stop retain the single-owner contract and serialized PhotoFrameController executor. No cross-thread caller guarantee, unknown-sound policy, synthesis/settings or audio quality redesign.",
    "Five baseline failures are Mockito WantedButNotInvoked/NeverWantedButInvoked verification failures. Full random-sample diagnostic printing was truncated and excluded; raw XML is bound. No full-stack or PCM-content review claim or excluded product rerun is made.",
    "Family frame review covers the current frame only. Living visual and physical soundscape UI remain open. Limited lines=1500 diagnostics do not establish complete runtime health.",
    "The original 13:35:36–14:05:36 UTC clock includes all inventory and delivery work. Date audit is bounded negative; CountdownDates/IrishHolidays 10:07:54 negatives, Prayer 07:01:27, TimerAlarm 08:51:50 and all older scopes keep their original clocks.",
    "Public manifest remains 1.83/code77. Existing phone-control, publication, HA and design-approval restrictions remain."
  ],
